From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:36:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 224/225] arm64: dts: ums512: disable pmsys rproc - CM4 stays
 behind stock lock

The SPL now ships with the stock CM4_SYS_SOFT_RST TZPC lock (SPL
CM4_DEFER dropped): the rproc's reset-release write is silently
ignored, the CM4 never runs, and rproc reports a phantom 'running'
with no SIPC channel ever opening. A75 DVFS does not need pm_sys.
Keep all the plumbing; flip status together with the SPL option if
the sensor hub is ever wired up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
index 242405650..9e30a5a17 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
@@ -533,9 +533,18 @@ soc: soc {
 		 *
 		 * dma-ranges is the CM4's view of the shared DDR and matches
 		 * the second smem-info triple, 0x88000000 -> 0x18000000.
+		 *
+		 * Disabled: the SPL ships with the stock CM4_SYS_SOFT_RST TZPC
+		 * lock (CONFIG_SPL_FW_CM4_DEFER off), so the reset-release
+		 * write is silently ignored and the CM4 never runs - booting
+		 * the rproc just reports a phantom "running". A75 DVFS does
+		 * NOT need pm_sys (it is serviced by the hw-i2c DVFS channels,
+		 * see i2c-sprd-hw.c). Re-enable together with the SPL defer if
+		 * the sensor hub is ever wired up.
 		 */
 		pmsys@800000 {
 			compatible = "sprd,ums512-pmsys";
+			status = "disabled";
 			reg = <0x0 0x800000 0x0 0x1000>;
 			dma-ranges = <0x18000000 0x0 0x88000000 0x08000000>;
 			#address-cells = <1>;
